    "title": "Why we might see Bill Murray at the Michigan State-UConn Sweet 16 game",
    "text": "Bill Murray tried to go incognito with a beard at a recent NCAA basketball game. But since he's one of the world's most recognizable comedic actors, it was really difficult to pull off.The actor, known for hit movie roles in \"Groundhog Day,\" \"Ghostbusters\" and \"Caddyshack\" and TV's \"Saturday Night Live,\" was spotted at the Connecticut-UCLA second round NCAA tournament game on Sunday, March 22, in Philadelphia. He also was at the UConn-Furman first-round game Friday, March 20.Actor Bill Murray reacts in the first half during a second round game of the men's 2026 NCAA Tournament at Xfinity Mobile Arena on Sunday, March 22, 2026 in Philadelphia.For UConn fans, this is nothing new. Murray was also present for the Huskies' back-to-back national championship runs in 2023 and 2024, on top of other postseason games. And it's a strong possibility he'll be in Washington when UConn takes on Michigan State basketball in the Sweet 16 on Friday, March 27 (9:45 p.m., CBS).AdvertisementWhy is Bill Murray a UConn fan?Murray's son, Luke, is an assistant coach at UConn, a No. 2 seed in this year's NCAA Tournament.Assistant coach Luke Murray of the Connecticut Huskies cuts down the net after beating the Purdue Boilermakers, 75-60, to win the NCAA Men's Basketball Tournament National Championship game at State Farm Stadium on April 8, 2024 in Glendale, Arizona.Luke Murray is in his fifth season on the UConn bench. Before taking the Huskies assistant job in 2021, he was an assistant at Xavier (2015-18) and Louisville (2018-21) under Chris Mack, now the College of Charleston coach. Luke Murray is in his ninth season on Hurley's staff across three different stops.This will be his last run with UConn, however; Murray was hired to run the Boston College basketball program on Thursday.Murray graduated from Fairfield University in 2007 in Connecticut and also served as an assistant coach at Post University (2008-09), Wagner (2010-11), Towson (2011-13) and Rhode Island (2013-15).AdvertisementON THE HARDWOOD: Scouting Michigan State basketball Sweet 16 matchup with UConnBill Murray eye to eye with a groundhog in a scene from the 1980 film \"Caddyshack.\"Where is Bill Murray from?Bill Murray grew up in Evanston, Illinois and was a fan of the Illini as a child. He moved to New York City in 1974 where he joined John Belushi on The National Lampoon Radio Hour – a comedy radio show that was created, produced and written by staff from National Lampoon magazine – before landing a spot on \"SNL.\" He attended Regis University in Denver, but dropped out before graduating.Bill Murray's 6 sonsAccording to People Magazine, Murray has six sons.Sons Homer, 43, and Luke, 40, are from his first wife Margaret Kelly, whom he was married to from 1981-96. Sons Caleb, 33, Jackson, 30, Cooper, 29, and Lincoln, 20, are with his second wife, Jennifer Butler. They split in 2008 after more than 10 years of marriage.AdvertisementFollow the Detroit Free Press on Instagram (@detroitfreepress), TikTok (@detroitfreepress), YouTube (@DetroitFreePress), Twitter/X (@freep), and LinkedIn, and like us on Facebook (@detroitfreepress).John Leuzzi of USA Today contributed to this story.Contact Amy Huschka: ahuschka@freepress.com or follow her on Twitter/X (@aetmanshuschka).Stay connected and stay informed. Become a subscriber.This article originally appeared on Detroit Free Press: Bill Murray at Michigan State-UConn game: Why we might see him",
